    "created_at": "2017-05-08T07:26:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-08T07:26:57Z",
    "body": "Between the two, I prefer the first option (some extension of \"disown the opener\" that breaks the link between the window and any references to its `WindowProxy`, perhaps along the lines of the discussion in the thread at https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-webappsec/2017Apr/0071.html). I agree that it would be a little annoying for history navigation, but I worry about making `WindowProxy` security checks too dynamic/expensive. I also think it's just simpler conceptually to consider a window that a user has taken control over as \"the user's window\" rather than \"the developer's window\".",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
